Files: Data/Recipes.lua and Data/QuestItems.lua, regenerated by tools/build-data.py (commit recorded in each header).
Forever Ledger itself credits Wago (client data), wow-classic-items (nexus-devs, MIT) and pfQuest (shagu, MIT).

Data/Recipes.lua also merges data from ProfessionsTracker 1.2.0 by Thork (https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/profession-tracker-forever),
which is under the MIT licence (Copyright (c) 2026 Thork; full text verbatim in THIRD-PARTY): the skill needed to learn each recipe, the
yellow / green / gray skill thresholds and some recipe sources, matched by English recipe name by tools/build-data.py. Data/Locations.lua
also vendors its trainer table, NPC positions and recipe "where" texts. Classic-era data,
not confirmed on Forever.

Data/ForeverRecipes.lua vendors the WoW Forever data of LibProfessionDB v1.10.1 by Pimptasty
(https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/professiondb), MIT licence (Copyright (c) 2026 Pimptasty; full text verbatim in THIRD-PARTY):
recipes, skill thresholds, reagents, required skills, teaching items, sources, vendor prices (build 1.60.1.70938). It is generated by
tools/build-lpdb.lua; no code of the library is shipped, and the ProfessionDB addon is not needed (and not used if installed).
Part of the sources are Vanilla values the library itself flags as borrowed; Gold Compass keeps those flags.

Data/ForeverTrainers.lua is generated by tools/fetch-wowforever.py from the per-profession recipe tables of wowforever.be
(https://wowforever.be/tradeskills/forever/<profession>/recipes/, build 1.60.1.70862): which recipes a trainer teaches on WoW Forever, the
trainer fee, the vendors and the recipes known from the start. It is in-game observed data; credit: wowforever.be. The site's robots.txt
allows these pages; the tool makes one request per page, two seconds apart, and the fetched HTML is cached outside the addon.

Learned.lua follows the approach of Forever Ledger's Professions.lua (read learned recipes when a profession window opens); no code was copied.

Data/Npcs.lua is generated by tools/build-npcs.py from pfQuest by shagu (https://github.com/shagu/pfQuest), MIT licence (Copyright (c)
2017-2021 Eric Mauser (Shagu); full text verbatim in THIRD-PARTY): the Classic spawn coordinates, faction and French names of the NPCs
Gold Compass can point to (profession trainers, recipe vendors and quest givers only). No code of pfQuest is shipped. The positions are the
original Classic ones; NPCs new to Forever are learned in game.

Data/ForeverNpcs.lua is generated by tools/build-foreverdb.py from the data files the ForeverDB addon publishes for addons and tools
(https://foreverdb.net, https://foreverdb.net/downloads/addon-manifest.json; game build 1.60.1.70959, data version 2026-11-18): where the
vendors and profession trainers of WoW Forever stand, with ForeverDB's own "seen in Forever" flag, which vendors sell each recipe and for
how much (gold or Merchant's Favor), the profession trainers, and the quests that reward a recipe with the place Forever players were
offered them. Data from ForeverDB.net. Licence of that data: GPL-3.0 with an attribution term (section 7(b): credit "Data from
ForeverDB.net"), see THIRD-PARTY. Gold Compass as a whole is therefore distributed under GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE); the MIT-licensed parts listed here
keep their own notices, as GPL-3.0 allows. The side of the quest
givers ForeverDB has no side for comes from pfQuest (MIT, above). No code of the ForeverDB addon is shipped.

Data/ForeverFixes.lua is generated by tools/build-forever-fixes.lua from the same ForeverDB.net data files (Recipes.lua): the recipe values
of the Forever client (skill needed, colour thresholds, crafted quantity, trainer fee) only where they differ from the other sources, and
the recipes that are not in the Forever client. Data from ForeverDB.net, same licence (GPL-3.0 with the attribution term).
Data/ForeverSkinning.lua is generated by tools/build-skinning.py from the same ForeverDB.net data (Gather.lua, Items.lua) and from
its public item pages (https://foreverdb.net/item/<id>, allowed by robots.txt, fetched 1.5 s apart): which skinnable beasts players
saw give each leather, hide and scale in WoW Forever, and where those beasts stand. Beasts without that Forever evidence come from
Classic data or a Classic level rule and are flagged as such. Data from ForeverDB.net, same licence (GPL-3.0 with the attribution term).
Data/ForeverSkinZones.lua is generated by tools/build-skin-zones.py: per zone, the skinnable beasts and their spawn points (Forever-seen
and Classic), from the same ForeverDB.net data (Gather.lua and the item pages). Data from ForeverDB.net, same licence (GPL-3.0 with the
attribution term). What one skin gives is Classic data from CMaNGOS classic-db (https://github.com/cmangos/classic-db, GPL-3.0:
creature_template and skinning_loot_template), flagged as not confirmed on Forever.
tools/audit-forever.lua compares everything Gold Compass shows with those files and with the owner's own SavedVariables.

Data/ForeverGather.lua is generated by tools/build-gather.py. Gathering locations: Data from ForeverDB.net (https://foreverdb.net), GPL-3.0; Classic points from CMaNGOS classic-db (GPL-3.0). Fishing zone skills: wowforever.be.

Data/ForeverRanks.lua is generated from ForeverDB.net data (ranks, Expert books and their vendors seen in Forever); Classic values are flagged. Data from ForeverDB.net, GPL-3.0 with the attribution term.

Data/ForeverReagentSources.lua is generated by tools/build-reagent-sources.py: Data from ForeverDB.net (https://foreverdb.net), GPL-3.0 with attribution term (section 7(b)). Classic vendor lists: pfQuest by Shagu (https://github.com/shagu/pfQuest), MIT licence; flagged as not seen in Forever.
